'''Melilotus sulcatus''', the '''furrowed melilot'''<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=13 June 2016 |df=dmy-all}}</ref> or '''Mediterranean sweetclover''',<ref>{{PLANTS|id=MESU2|taxon=Melilotus sulcatus|accessdate=13 June 2016}}</ref> is a species of the [[genus]] ''[[Melilotus]]'', belonging to the [[pea]] family; [[Fabaceae]] or [[Papilionaceae]].

It is distributed in Southern Europe, an annual plant between {{Convert abbreviated|10 and 40|cm|sigfig=2}} high. The stem leaves are grooved. The flowers are very small; 3–5&nbsp;mm long, in bloom  from June until August. The pods are 3–3.5&nbsp;mm long, with bowline veins.

